<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hancheng</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hancheng is a county-level city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>. It is the traditional birthplace of the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-qian">Sima Qian</a>, whose temple and tomb stand there, and its old town keeps many Ming and Qing buildings. Excavations at Liangdai village nearby uncovered rich tombs of the Zhou-period State of Rui.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hancheng.jpg" alt="Hancheng" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Cshcts on zh.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dangjiacun.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
